# std/grep (design/caos-expr.md): this directory built by rustc, with the built
# rgrep image curried on as the fold it runs. The help is a HERE-STRING so it
# lives in this expression, which is stripped from the tree the build sees.
HELP=<<END
Search with a regular expression (Rust regex syntax, line-based). `root` is what to search: a file, a directory or a source tree in the session (`.` for all of it), or `<hash>[/<path>]` for one that is not in the session, such as an evaluated caos-std/. Returns matches as `path:linenum:line`, paths relative to root. Results are cached per unchanged subtree, so repeated and narrow searches are cheap. Output is cut at 100KB, with the number of files left out. Prefer this over grep or find via bash.
@param pattern The regular expression to search for.
@root
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=.
curry --base=$IMAGE --rgrep:@=DEEP-DEPS/rgrep --help=$HELP
